Root cause:
The bug was caused by improper handling of RCU (Read-Copy-Update) dereferences for the `from` field in the `rt6_info` structure. Specifically, the code was accessing the `from` pointer without ensuring that it was properly dereferenced using `rcu_dereference`, which can lead to accessing stale or invalid data if the `from` pointer is modified concurrently. This oversight could result in undefined behavior or crashes in the networking code, particularly when the RCU lock was not held during the access. The patch addresses this by ensuring that `rcu_dereference_protected` is used correctly and that a reference is taken on `from` before it is accessed outside of the RCU lock.
